// Increment 3: the tractor-semitrailer constant-radius runtime fixture.
//
// One 80 m-radius quarter-circle guide path (120 chords — finer than the
// `heavy_turning_v2`/`narrow_isolated_curve_v2` 24-chord convention, because
// the trailer's hitch angle responds to each chord's *heading* discontinuity,
// not only its position sagitta, and a coarser chording measurably ripples the
// steady-state comparison below), carrying
// only the `tractor_semitrailer` mode template — the only vehicle on its path,
// so no collision partner is needed to prove pose correctness
// (tas-12mx01cfsxskm0pjzq13hvcm2g). The template authors no `wheelbase_m`/
// `steering_angle_max_rad`, so the compiler's turning-limit/facility-curvature
// check (`mode_turning_limit_curvature`) does not apply to it: off-tracking and
// corner-curvature validation under articulation are a sibling node's, per
// scope.
//
// The 80 m radius is chosen so the quarter-circle sweep gives the trailer's
// hitch-angle transient several arm-length time constants (`L/v`) to relax
// toward its steady state before the run ends: `crates/hekate-sim/tests/
// inc3_articulated.rs` holds the settled hitch angle to the classical
// single-axle trailer steady-state off-tracking formula, `sin(phi) = L / R`.
